      "message": "Does this run even when running tests locally during development? If so, that could slow things down a bit. On cuttlefish, \"time adb shell dumpsys connectivity --dump-priority HIGH\" reports 100-200ms real time, which is probably fine. But on my physical device it took almost 6 seconds because it tried to test the IMS network which doeesn\u0027t respond to our probes, and because it attempted DoT to the carrier\u0027s DNS servers which don\u0027t support DoT.\n\nMaybe add a TODO somewhere to provide a way to pass a lower timeout to dumpsys, or to only run tests that we expect to succeed (e.g., only test INTERNET networks, don\u0027t test DoT unless in strict mode, etc.)?",
